{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0dcf51a6-38d3-412b-94f8-fe9fdd0fca16","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b61e9fc51330f736","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-g5n6ydpn/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8009 — Workspace-aware artifact serving for multi-tenant MLflow deployments\n\n## Triage Result\n\nNot triaged as below-threshold or docs-only. The strategy is Critical priority, M-L effort (4–7 sprints), and spans three architecturally distinct sub-systems (Python MLflow server, Go MLflow operator, mlflow-kubernetes-plugins package) that warrant separate PR review cycles, with multiple genuine unknowns (4 open questions, 5 assumptions marked \"needs validation\"). Full decomposition follows.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input Handling\n\nThe Staff Engineer / SME Input section is non-empty and takes precedence. All three corrections are already incorporated into the strategy's Technical Approach; no overrides were required:\n\n- **No new flag** — the approach combines existing `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` flags; the strategy body contains no reference to `--artifacts-only-workspace-aware` or `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware`. The server and operator epics carry this constraint explicitly in scope.\n- **Operator work is a split deployment, not a config toggle** — the operator epic delivers a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute plus artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment.\n- **SSAR detail over-specified** — the epics state that workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure without dictating Kubernetes API mechanics (no SSAR/pseudo-resource prescriptions appear in any epic scope).\n\n## Component Mapping\n\nCanonical RHAI component list (`.context/rhai-components.txt`) contains