AT-8009-E008 | End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving | Implementation | MLflow Team | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: plugin workspace-resolution coupling\"] --> E004[\"E004 Plugin workspace resolution for artifacts-only context\"]\n    E004 --> E003[\"E003 Server: workspace-aware artifacts-only serving\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Investigation: artifact traffic routing design\"] --> E005[\"E005 Operator: split-server topology\"]\n    E003 --> E008[\"E008 End-to-end integration validation\"]\n    E004 --> E008\n    E005 --> E008\n    E003 --> E007[\"E007 Audit logging for access denials\"]\n    E006[\"E006 Investigation: audit telemetry channel\"] --> E007\n```\n\nRoots: E001, E002, E006 (all three start in parallel). Critical path: E001 → E004 → E003 → E008 (4 epics).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | The plugin-coupling investigation determines the plugin epic's scope: verification only (not coupled) vs. refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path (coupled). True gate — `rewrite`. |\n| E004 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact another epic builds against) | The plugin is a library the server loads; the server's new artifact-request validation code builds against the plugin's workspace resolution. Consuming implementation is serial after the library. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | The routing design investigation determines the operator epic's approach (gateway-level routing vs. main-deployment delegation, and whether the tracking server needs a configuration change). True gate — `rewrite`. |\n| E003 → E008 | Rule 13 / integration consumption | Integration validation exercises the server capability end to end. |\n| E004 → E008 | Rule 13 / integration consumption | Integration validation exercises plugin workspace resolution in the deployed topology. |\n| E005 → E008 | Rule 13 / integration consumption | Split-server routing scenarios require the operator-deployed topology. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 13 | Audit logging instruments the workspace-denial code path the server epic creates; it builds on that surface. |\n| E006 → E007 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | The channel decision (server logs vs. OTLP vs. Kubernetes audit log) determines the audit implementation's scope. True gate — `rewrite`. |\n\nDeliberate **non-edges** (parallelism):\n\n| Pair | Rule | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| E005 ∥ E003/E004 | Rule 13 (configuration references are AC gates) | The operator renders the flag combination into Deployment templates — a configuration reference to the server's capability, not a build-against artifact. Coupling is expressed as an AC on E005 (\"rendered topology verified against a workspace-aware artifacts-only server build\") and validated end to end in E008. |\n| E002 chain ∥ E001 chain | Rule 14 (different repos/sub-systems) | Operator routing design is independent of server/plugin workspace resolution work. |\n| E006 ∥ all | Rule 14 | The audit channel decision (PM/Security) blocks only the P2 audit implementation. |\n| E007 ∥ E008 | Rule 15 | Audit logging (P2) does not gate integration validation of the P0/P1 capability. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri` for workspace-validated artifact serving | P0 | E003 (implementation), E008 (validation) | |\n| Artifact requests validated against workspace membership; non-members denied HTTP 403 | P0 | E003 (implementation), E004 (enabling), E008 (validation) | |\n| Fail-closed: workspace store unreachable → requests denied | P0 | E003 (implementation), E008 (validation) | |\n| Single-tenant / no-workspace-flag deployments retain current behavior | P0 | E003 (implementation + regression ACs), E008 (regression validation) | |\n| Operator deploys