 covering member and non-member outcomes\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace lookup) is demonstrated to function in a server context with no tracking store or model registry store initialization\n- If coupling to the full server initialization path was found, workspace resolution is factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin and the refactoring is covered by tests\n- Workspace resolution resolves artifact-request context to a workspace assignment with correct member/non-member results in tests\n- No change is required to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar or `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\n- Note on priority: the HLR is labeled P1 in the strategy, but this epic is P0 by priority inheritance — workspace resolution enables the P0 membership-validation and fail-closed HLRs delivered by the server-side workspace-aware artifact serving work\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88822,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b34a512e1b7fc615","agent_id":"a8c8fab44d11c6743","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"2f554c79-8444-4546-819d-04fd7ba411fd","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:22:02.023Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
