design investigation)\n- Create the artifacts-only instance's Gateway API HTTPRoute conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies\n- Operator validation: reject configurations where the artifacts-only instance would run without the workspace flags when workspace-aware artifact serving is intended, so misconfiguration cannot silently bypass workspace validation\n- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, it creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations\n- The dedicated artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec\n- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design\n- The artifacts-only instance's HTTPRoute is created only when Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime (conditional dependency preserved)\n- The operator rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance would lack workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is intended\n- Deployments that do not enable the split topology reconcile unchanged (backwards compatibility)\n- The rendered topology is verified against a workspace-aware artifacts-only server build (a server image supporting the combined flags) — an acceptance gate on this epic, not a build dependency on the server work\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\n- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89474,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b34a512e1b7fc615","agent_id":"a8c8fab44d11c6743","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"0fe66516-1fb4-487a-a7b9-4aa310f63c6d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:22:12.909Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
