e is identified so the audit logging work can be scoped from it\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Resolves the strategy's open question \"Should workspace access denials generate audit events through a specific telemetry channel (OTLP, Kubernetes audit log, server log)?\"\n- Gates the [P2] HLR \"Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs\" — the channel choice determines what the audit implementation builds\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90329,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b34a512e1b7fc615","agent_id":"a8c8fab44d11c6743","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"ba89ddbb-a7a9-4786-8ddc-cf833bbc0295","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:22:21.619Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
