{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2f39af0f154c46e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server MLflow topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server MLflow topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermine how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy leaves this as an open question owned by the MLflow team: the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome selects the routing mechanism the operator's split-server topology implementation will build.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate routing options: gateway-level routing of artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance (for example path-based HTTPRoute rules) versus configuring the main tracking deployment to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance\n34\t- Determine whether the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, or whether routing can be handled entirely at the gateway layer\n35\t- Assess the implications for the dedicated instance's HTTPRoute design and for the operator's existing conditional Gateway API CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies\n36\t- Verify that kube-rbac-proxy sidecar authentication behavior is identical whichever routing mechanism is selected (authentication at ingress is unchanged for both server types, per Staff Engineer input)\n37\t- Deliver a design decision documenting the selected routing mechanism, its constraints, and what configuration the main tracking deployment needs\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A routing design decision is documented, selecting the mechanism for routing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n42\t- The decision states explicitly whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and what that change is\n43\t- The HTTPRoute design for the dedicated instance (and any main-deployment routing configuration) is specified at the level the operator implementation can build against\n44\t- The decision is consistent with the operator's existing conditional Gateway API CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies\n45\t- The decision confirms ingress authentication (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) is unaffected by the chosen mechanism\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- Resolves the strategy's open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\"\n50\t- Gates the HLRs \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" (P1) and \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" (P1)\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"b8e2dee1-3797-41ca-9ad7-843b6a122dba","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:36.403Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2f39af0f154c46e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
