{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc10ee9b198848d5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tMake the MLflow tracking server's `--artifacts-only` mode composable with `--enable-workspaces` so that artifact serving is validated against workspace membership in multi-tenant deployments. When both flags are set, the server requires an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`, initializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests, and leaves tracking stores, model registry stores, and non-artifact API endpoints uninitialized and disabled. Per Staff Engineer input, no new server flag is introduced — the workspace-aware behavior emerges from combining the two existing flags, and no reference to a separate workspace-aware artifact flag or CR field may be reintroduced.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Compose `--artifacts-only` with `--enable-workspaces`: when both are set, require an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`; fail to start with a clear error if it is missing\n39\t- Initialize only the workspace provider in artifacts-only mode; keep tracking and model registry stores uninitialized and non-artifact API endpoints disabled\n40\t- Add workspace validation to artifact request handling: resolve the artifact path to its parent experiment (artifacts are stored under experiment-scoped paths, e.g. `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), look up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegate authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure — without dictating Kubernetes API mechanics inside the plugin\n41\t- Deny requests from users without workspace membership with HTTP 403 and an error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions\n42\t- Fail closed: if the workspace store is unreachable while workspace-aware mode is active, deny artifact requests (HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable) rather than serving without validation\n43\t- Preserve current behavior when either flag is absent: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces` serves artifacts without workspace validation, and deployments that do not set workspace flags are unaffected\n44\t- Implement short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions, consistent with caching patterns already used in the tracking server's auth path, to bound the per-request latency of workspace resolution\n45\t- Scope initial artifact path resolution to the S3 artifact store (the standard RHOAI configuration, where paths follow the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure) and document limitations for non-standard artifact roots\n46\t- Measure and report the per-request latency overhead added by workspace validation\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given the artifacts-only instance started with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://` and a user who is a member of workspace A, when the user requests an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace A, then the artifact is served — measured by HTTP 200 with correct artifact content\n51\t- Given the same deployment and a user who is a member of workspace A but not workspace B, when the user requests an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace B, then the request is denied — measured by HTTP 403 with an error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions\n52\t- Given `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, when any authenticated user requests an artifact, then it is served without workspace validation — measured by HTTP 200 regardless of workspace membership (current behavior preserved)\n53\t- Given workspace-aware mode active and the workspace store (Kubernetes API) unreachable, when a user requests an artifact, then the request is denied — measured by HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable (fail-closed)\n54\t- Given `--enable-workspaces` set with `--artifacts-only` but no `--workspace-store-uri`, the server fails to start with a clear error\n55\t- Single-tenant deployments and configurations without workspace flags retain current behavior, covered by regression tests\n56\t- The per-request latency overhead of workspace validation is measured and reported against the latency budget agreed with PM/Engineering\n57\t- Limitations of artifact path resolution for non-standard artifact roots are documented\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- [P0] `--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri` to enable workspace-validated artifact serving\n62\t- [P0] Artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\n63\t- [P0] Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed: if the workspace store is unreachable, requests are denied\n64\t- [P0] Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior with no changes\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"76dd74e7-f69d-474a-a4b3-0e773ea93c31","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:36.959Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc10ee9b198848d5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
