{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9221f0d51b787904","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Artifact-context workspace resolution in the MLflow Kubernetes plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds workspace resolution is not coupled\n15\t    to tracking store initialization, this epic reduces to verification and test coverage\n16\t    in the artifacts-only context; if coupled, it includes refactoring workspace resolution\n17\t    into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Artifact-context workspace resolution in the MLflow Kubernetes plugins\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tVerify and extend the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin so that workspace resolution — the experiment-to-workspace mapping provided by the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group — functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. If the workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor it into an independent initialization path within the plugin so the artifacts-only server can call the same workspace resolution logic before serving or proxying artifact requests.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution works when initialized in the artifacts-only context: workspace store only, no tracking store or model registry store initialization\n44\t- If the investigation into the plugin's initialization dependencies finds coupling to tracking store availability, refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin\n45\t- Ensure workspace resolution is callable with artifact-request context (the experiment ID resolved from the artifact path) and returns the workspace assignment the server's authorization check needs\n46\t- Keep the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup unchanged — authentication at the ingress level works identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance (Staff Engineer input)\n47\t- Add test coverage for workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context, covering member and non-member outcomes\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace lookup) is demonstrated to function in a server context with no tracking store or model registry store initialization\n52\t- If coupling to the full server initialization path was found, workspace resolution is factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin and the refactoring is covered by tests\n53\t- Workspace resolution resolves artifact-request context to a workspace assignment with correct member/non-member results in tests\n54\t- No change is required to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar or `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P1] Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\n59\t- Note on priority: the HLR is labeled P1 in the strategy, but this epic is P0 by priority inheritance — workspace resolution enables the P0 membership-validation and fail-closed HLRs delivered by the server-side workspace-aware artifact serving work\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"4c32baf5-fb8a-4d72-9e8b-324960c99428","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:37.481Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9221f0d51b787904","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
