{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86c36eefe3e5180f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifact serving topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design selects gateway-level routing, artifact\n15\t    traffic is routed via HTTPRoute rules with no main tracking deployment change;\n16\t    if the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations,\n17\t    the main deployment configuration and routing templates are rewritten to that\n18\t    design.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Split-server artifact serving topology in the MLflow operator\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to route artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology, not a single-deployment configuration toggle (Staff Engineer input). The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. Users configure a single MLflow CR and the operator manages the topology declaratively.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute\n45\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`, `--serve-artifacts`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment, combining `--artifacts-only` with the workspace flags — no new CR field of the form `spec.artifactsOnly.workspaceAware` (per Staff Engineer input, workspace-aware behavior comes from flag composition)\n46\t- Configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design (gateway-level routing or main-deployment delegation, as determined by the routing design investigation)\n47\t- Create the artifacts-only instance's Gateway API HTTPRoute conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies\n48\t- Operator validation: reject configurations where the artifacts-only instance would run without the workspace flags when workspace-aware artifact serving is intended, so misconfiguration cannot silently bypass workspace validation\n49\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, it creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations\n54\t- The dedicated artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec\n55\t- Artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design\n56\t- The artifacts-only instance's HTTPRoute is created only when Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime (conditional dependency preserved)\n57\t- The operator rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance would lack workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is intended\n58\t- Deployments that do not enable the split topology reconcile unchanged (backwards compatibility)\n59\t- The rendered topology is verified against a workspace-aware artifacts-only server build (a server image supporting the combined flags) — an acceptance gate on this epic, not a build dependency on the server work\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- [P1] MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\n64\t- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"9224b89b-1982-4aee-8240-3aa8cdd44a2c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:41.205Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86c36eefe3e5180f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
