{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-907cd7290ff7a3c0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Decide the audit telemetry channel for workspace access denials\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide the audit telemetry channel for workspace access denials\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDecide through which telemetry channel workspace access denials in artifact serving should generate audit events: server logs (the baseline stated in the strategy's P2 requirement), OTLP telemetry, or the Kubernetes audit log. The strategy leaves this question to PM/Security with technical feasibility input from the MLflow team; the answer determines the scope of the audit logging implementation. This is a decision investigation: the gating question is a governance decision the MLflow team cannot make alone.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Frame the decision: auditability requirements for workspace access denials in multi-tenant artifact serving — who consumes the events, retention needs, and correlation with other security events\n34\t- Assess the feasibility and cost of each candidate channel: server log emission, OTLP export through the existing observability stack, and Kubernetes audit log integration\n35\t- Record the PM/Security decision with rationale, including whether server logs alone satisfy the requirement or an additional channel is required\n36\t- Specify the audit event content required (identity, workspace, experiment, decision) at the level the audit logging implementation can build against\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A documented decision selects the audit channel(s) for workspace access denials in artifact serving, with PM/Security sign-off recorded\n41\t- The decision specifies the audit event content and the channel(s) the implementation must emit to\n42\t- If the decision extends beyond server logs, the additional integration scope is identified so the audit logging work can be scoped from it\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Resolves the strategy's open question \"Should workspace access denials generate audit events through a specific telemetry channel (OTLP, Kubernetes audit log, server log)?\"\n47\t- Gates the [P2] HLR \"Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs\" — the channel choice determines what the audit implementation builds\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"b6d7dd9d-2045-406f-89a8-a446ffa19264","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:42.365Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-907cd7290ff7a3c0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
