t emission through the selected channel — server logs by default, plus any additional channel the audit channel decision requires\n46\t- Emit denial audit events at a severity consistent with security-relevant events in the server's existing logging conventions\n47\t- Add test coverage: denial events are emitted for both membership denials and fail-closed denials\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Every workspace access denial in artifact serving (HTTP 403 membership denial and HTTP 503 fail-closed denial) produces an audit record through the selected channel\n52\t- Audit records contain the requesting identity, workspace, experiment, and decision\n53\t- Denial audit emission is covered by tests for both denial modes\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- [P2] Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs (channel per the audit channel decision)\n58\t- Note on split: this work is separated from the P0 server implementation because the audit channel is an open question whose answer changes what gets built; it instruments the denial path the server implementation creates rather than building a second surface\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"005482d7-0923-41af-b204-a100f6876aa5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:43.074Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a106844c09a35f09","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
