{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a39a53ffe3f996","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n3\ttitle: End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: 0\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\timplementation_type: null\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 5\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# End-to-end integration validation of workspace-aware artifact serving\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tValidate the assembled workspace-aware artifact serving capability end to end across the split-server topology: the workspace-aware artifacts-only server, the auth plugin's workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context, and the operator-deployed dedicated instance with artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment. This is the strategy's dedicated integration testing effort — multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed edge cases, and split-server routing.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Multi-tenant workspace scenarios through the operator-deployed topology: member of the owning workspace is served (HTTP 200, correct content); non-member is denied (HTTP 403)\n41\t- Fail-closed edge cases: workspace store (Kubernetes API) unreachable yields denials (HTTP 503), never silent degradation of tenant isolation\n42\t- Single-tenant regression and backwards compatibility: deployments without workspace flags, and artifacts-only mode without `--enable-workspaces`, retain current behavior\n43\t- Split-server routing: artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment reaches the dedicated artifacts-only instance; operator validation rejects misconfigured topologies (artifacts-only instance lacking workspace flags)\n44\t- Artifact path resolution end to end on the S3 artifact store (the standard RHOAI configuration, `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure)\n45\t- Capture test results and evidence mapping each strategy acceptance criterion to its observed result\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- All multi-tenant workspace scenarios pass through the operator-deployed split topology (member served with correct content; non-member denied with HTTP 403)\n50\t- Fail-closed behavior is verified: workspace store unreachability produces denials (HTTP 503), not unvalidated serves\n51\t- Single-tenant and no-workspace-flag regression scenarios pass (current behavior preserved)\n52\t- Artifact traffic routing between the main tracking deployment and the dedicated artifacts-only instance is verified end to end\n53\t- A validation report maps each strategy acceptance criterion to its observed result\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Validation coverage for [P0] workspace-validated artifact serving, [P0] membership denial (HTTP 403), [P0] fail-closed behavior, [P0] backwards compatibility, [P1] dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment, and [P1] artifact traffic routing — the implementing epics own these HLRs; this epic validates them end to end\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1b800ebeb3e27f","agent_id":"ad67cdf5ce146e70e","session_id":"1dcc8d9d-3485-4c95-9a3d-f9307d0024ef","uuid":"ed3310e9-cab9-4fc5-8f6c-7df2598fa50e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:25:43.628Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a39a53ffe3f996","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","